# 7. What is an Attack Surface?

The **attack surface** is the collection of possible entry points through which an application can be interacted with or potentially attacked.

For a web application:

```text
Attack Surface
├── Login
├── Registration
├── Search
├── File Upload
├── Forms
├── APIs
├── Admin Panel
├── Cookies
├── Headers
└── URL Parameters
```

### Memory

> **Attack Surface = Places where input enters or functionality is exposed.**

